{
  "id": "COMPOUND:14279 - PROTEIN:5836",
  "verbalization": "Budesonide is implicated in the interaction with HUVEC through a series of molecular pathways, with the target entity consistently identified as Thioredoxin, mitochondrial. This protein is targeted by multiple compounds, including Spathelia bischromene, Yuanhunine, and Oleamide, all of which are themselves targets of budesonide. The shared involvement of Thioredoxin, mitochondrial in these relationships suggests a potential mechanism by which budesonide influences HUVEC function. The evidence points to a possible role of Thioredoxin, mitochondrial in mediating the effects of these compounds on HUVEC, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular network linking budesonide to HUVEC, emphasizing the need for further investigation into the specific mechanisms involved.",
